      "writtenOn": "2023-10-27T18:23:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not just use the current doc string contents in `VerifyErrorCode`? Or just print out the name of the enum variant? That would be much more consistent and avoid the subtly incorrect terms introduced below. Having a totally separate set of descriptions for the same set of errors will only increase confusion.",
      "revId": "3e308e9a5621ccbf335a8abc2ce4f05a59f44ef7",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "12e8d69d_32047c74",
        "filename": "extra/usb_updater/gsctool.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 4352,
      "author": {
        "id": 1541362
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-27T18:23:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s not just a \"wrong\" key, it\u0027s a key that isn\u0027t structured correctly. I would call it a `Bad key` or `Inconsistent key`, not a `Wrong key`, since that implies it could be returned if the value is signed validly with a key that the system doesn\u0027t recognize.\n\nSo, don\u0027t say \"Wrong\", because these errors are about the item itself being incorrectly structured instead of having a correctly structured, but incorrectly chosen, item.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4352,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 4352,
        "endChar": 8
      },
      "revId": "3e308e9a5621ccbf335a8abc2ce4f05a59f44ef7",
